(*
expect:
a2d827617a01d82762616102
*)
(* Rung 3 Task 5: Cbor encode deterministic map order. Keys #z -> 1, #aa -> 2.
   The algebra Map stores keys in valueCompare order (over printString '#z' vs
   '#aa'), which sorts #aa BEFORE #z. But RFC 8949 bytewise order over the
   ENCODED keys sorts #z (d827617a) BEFORE #aa (d827626161) — they diverge
   because the keys differ in encoded length. The encoder must re-sort at emit
   time; the golden is the bytewise-sorted form, so this fails if the walk emits
   in the Map's stored (valueCompare) order.
   Golden authored independently from python cbor2 6.1.3 (see 14_cbor/README.md);
   cbor2 canonical == explicit RFC 8949 bytewise sort. *)
class CborMapOrderTest packageUsing: manifest = () (
public main: platform args: args = (
  | M m |
  M:: platform Map.
  m:: M with: #z -> 1 with: #aa -> 2.
  (platform Cbor encode: m) printHex println.
)
) : (
)
